to get those pants clean.

246
00:09:44,252 --> 00:09:46,720
- Yes, but how will they erase
the shame of this movie?

247
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:47,755
- Ooh.

248
00:09:49,290 --> 00:09:51,358
- Whoa!
Hah, well, at this point,
what's inappropriate?

249
00:09:51,392 --> 00:09:52,827
Ha, ha!

250
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:55,963
- Unreleased footage
from The Piano.

251
00:09:55,997 --> 00:09:58,332
- Couldn't they
have used all this time
to show short scenes

252
00:09:58,365 --> 00:10:01,102
of their growing discontent
with society's morey's?

253
00:10:01,135 --> 00:10:03,103
- Well, they got a lot
of wet boob shots in.

254
00:10:03,137 --> 00:10:04,838
- Hey.

255
00:10:04,872 --> 00:10:07,240
- Must, get to, busted, sign.

256
00:10:09,008 --> 00:10:10,712
- Hey!
- Oh! We have dialog!

257
00:10:10,745 --> 00:10:12,780
- Let's go to Hainesville
to have some fun, huh?

258
00:10:12,813 --> 00:10:14,782
- What have you been doing?
- Yeah, but how are we

259
00:10:14,815 --> 00:10:15,850
gonna get there?

260
00:10:15,883 --> 00:10:17,385
- Those long, long legs, baby!

261
00:10:17,418 --> 00:10:20,722
- Ah, three miles,
are you kidding?!

262
00:10:20,755 --> 00:10:22,957
- Hey, it's a wild idea,
let's go down to the 'go-go's'

263
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:24,725
and cause
a little trouble, huh?

264
00:10:24,758 --> 00:10:27,027
- Are you serious?
That's three miles away!

265
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:29,697
- Oh, baby,
it'll be good for ya!

266
00:10:29,730 --> 00:10:31,732
- Harry, the overnight bags!
- Yes, Madam.

267
00:10:31,765 --> 00:10:33,667
- Hey, besides,
there's this broad down there

268
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:35,402
I've always had my eye on,
what's her name?

269
00:10:35,435 --> 00:10:37,705
- Koruba!
- Nancy! N-Nancy or something

270
00:10:37,738 --> 00:10:39,005
or the w-w-wait a minute--

271
00:10:39,038 --> 00:10:40,875
- Oo, that's not mud. Oo!

272
00:10:40,908 --> 00:10:42,342
- Oo.

273
00:10:42,375 --> 00:10:44,812
♪ [Instrumental Version
of 'Marianne' Playing] ♪

274
00:10:44,845 --> 00:10:48,215
- ♪ A summer place ♪

275
00:10:48,248 --> 00:10:50,050
♪ A summer place ♪

276
00:10:50,083 --> 00:10:52,085
- [As Announcer]
Model home may not be available

277
00:10:52,118 --> 00:10:54,822
as seen.

278
00:10:54,855 --> 00:10:58,058
- Pretty nice system,
that's a Thorens Turntable
with a Conrad-Johnson Amp.

279
00:10:58,092 --> 00:10:59,360
Stasis Class A.

280
00:10:59,393 --> 00:11:02,162
- Ozzie & Harriet,
after dark. [Growls]

281
00:11:02,195 --> 00:11:04,165
- This is Tommy Kirk
really acting.

282
00:11:04,198 --> 00:11:06,100
- Ooh.

283
00:11:06,133 --> 00:11:08,168
- [As Dog]
I'm next. Ruff.

284
00:11:08,202 --> 00:11:11,438
- Ugh.
- Ew!

285
00:11:11,472 --> 00:11:13,773
- Even the dog's grossed out!

286
00:11:13,807 --> 00:11:16,177
- [Disgusting Slurping Noises]

287
00:11:18,478 --> 00:11:19,880
- Uh-oh.

288
00:11:19,913 --> 00:11:21,982
- When do your parents
get back in town?

289
00:11:22,015 --> 00:11:23,917
- They're spending the night
in Los Angeles.

290
00:11:23,950 --> 00:11:25,218
- [Deep Voice]
Oh, yeah...

291
00:11:25,252 --> 00:11:26,987
[Speaking French]

292
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:28,322
Oh, that's French.

293
00:11:28,355 --> 00:11:30,323
- There's a big landslide
up the road.

294
00:11:30,357 --> 00:11:32,225
- A landslide?

295
00:11:32,258 --> 00:11:35,462
- Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.
- I bet you are.

296
00:11:35,495 --> 00:11:38,865
- So, what's for dinner?
- Hey, Mike!

297
00:11:38,898 --> 00:11:40,200
- Look what I got.
- Eeewww.

298
00:11:40,233 --> 00:11:43,937
- Am2Su, HCSoF,
and Magnesium Sulfate.

299
00:11:43,970 --> 00:11:45,372
How about that, Mike?

300
00:11:45,405 --> 00:11:47,307
- It's very impressive,
Genius.

301
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:49,177
- They're not compatible.
- Like you guys.

302
00:11:49,210 --> 00:11:51,345
- This is supposed to blow up.

303
00:11:51,378 --> 00:11:53,147
- I wonder why it doesn't.
- Poor Ron.

304
00:11:53,180 --> 00:11:55,783
- You and I aren't going to be
very compatible either Genius,

305
00:11:55,817 --> 00:11:57,317
if you don't get out of here.

306
00:11:57,350 --> 00:12:00,087
- I hope that
blows up in his face so I
don't have to see Willow.

307
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,888
- Hey, I liked Willow.

308
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:06,293
- Crash! Agh! Clastic liquid
all over my face! Agh!

309
00:12:06,327 --> 00:12:08,528
- I don't know either.
But, uh, whatever it is,

310
00:12:08,562 --> 00:12:10,097
I like it.

311
00:12:10,130 --> 00:12:12,365
- Oh, take me,
you savage Mouseketeer.

312
00:12:12,398 --> 00:12:15,002
- Oh, you're good for me,
Nancy, you know that?

313
00:12:15,035 --> 00:12:17,838
- Uh-uh.
- Oh, you are very, very good.

314
00:12:17,872 --> 00:12:19,840
- But I'm afraid
I'm gonna have to fire you.

315
00:12:19,873 --> 00:12:21,042
Cut-backs.

316
00:12:21,075 --> 00:12:22,943
- I never knew
you liked good girls.

317
00:12:22,977 --> 00:12:25,378
- I don't.
They talk too much.

318
00:12:25,412 --> 00:12:26,847
- And they smell weird!

319
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,115
- So?

320
00:12:28,148 --> 00:12:30,517
- So, stop talking so much.

321
00:12:30,550 --> 00:12:32,553
- Did you have
Kung Pao Chicken?

322
00:12:32,587 --> 00:12:34,120
[Explosion, Crashing Sound]

323
00:12:34,153 --> 00:12:36,257
- Aaaa, Aunt Bea,
I can't find my legs!

324
00:12:36,290 --> 00:12:38,192
- Help me!
- [Laughter]

325
00:12:40,427 --> 00:12:42,530
- I flip, I flip,
I flip, flip. Flip!

326
00:12:50,437 --> 00:12:52,205
- [As Jerry Lewis]
Hoiman, hoiman!

327
00:12:52,238 --> 00:12:54,007
[Coughs]

328
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:55,308
[Grumbles]

329
00:12:58,578 --> 00:13:00,982
- Honey, I shrunk the Opie.
- Boing!

330
00:13:01,015 --> 00:13:02,917
- I blinded me with Science!

331
00:13:04,918 --> 00:13:07,153
- That's not really
what I was trying to do.

332
00:13:07,187 --> 00:13:08,855
- Genius,
are you all right?

333
00:13:08,888 --> 00:13:10,423
- [As Genius]
Suddenly I want to direct.

334
00:13:10,457 --> 00:13:12,893
- Of course I'm all right.
Why shouldn't I be?

335
00:13:12,927 --> 00:13:15,062
- Well,
you could've been killed.

336
00:13:15,095 --> 00:13:17,163
- Oh, nonsense.
- [Mild Screeching Sound]

337
00:13:17,197 --> 00:13:18,832
- Well, you could have.

338
00:13:18,865 --> 00:13:21,302
- I put an electric charge
to that stuff I was mixing,

339
00:13:21,335 --> 00:13:23,003
- and then-- Pow!--
- I am so ashamed.

340
00:13:23,037 --> 00:13:24,438
- --the whole place blew up!

341
00:13:24,472 --> 00:13:26,373
- Hm, Tommy's not too hard
to entertain.

342
00:13:26,407 --> 00:13:27,942
- Hah, hah, no.

343
00:13:29,877 --> 00:13:32,078
- Nice of Tommy
to stay awake for this scene.

344
00:13:32,112 --> 00:13:33,613
- I wonder what that is.

345
00:13:33,647 --> 00:13:37,350
- [As Mike]
I wonder what 'The King"
is doing tonight?

346
00:13:37,383 --> 00:13:40,153
- Do you think it might be
ammonia-astride sulfate?

347
00:13:42,088 --> 00:13:45,893
- No. It's either pancake mix,
or an octopus.

348
00:13:45,927 --> 00:13:47,628
- [Small Chuckles]
- Don't try to be funny.

349
00:13:47,662 --> 00:13:49,230
- What a relief.

350
00:13:51,098 --> 00:13:53,600
- [As Dr. Strangelove]
Mein Fuehrer, I can walk! Arf!

351
00:13:54,968 --> 00:13:57,070
- Yes, but what does it mean?!

352
00:13:57,103 --> 00:13:59,607
- Hey, Thomasina!
- Don't get that cat involved.

353
00:13:59,640 --> 00:14:01,475
- Please.

354
00:14:01,508 --> 00:14:04,245
- A mess.

355
00:14:04,278 --> 00:14:06,147
All right Genius,
put your talents

356
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:08,348
to cleaning this up.
Go get a broom.

357
00:14:10,117 --> 00:14:12,518
- Things
this kid comes up with.
Fantastic!

358
00:14:12,552 --> 00:14:14,422
- Fan-tas-tic.
- I suppose.

359
00:14:14,455 --> 00:14:17,090
Anyway,
he does keep things
from getting dull,

360
00:14:17,123 --> 00:14:18,658
if he just
wouldn't overdo it.

361
00:14:18,692 --> 00:14:20,460
- Mm, you can taste
the codfish flavor!

362
00:14:20,493 --> 00:14:22,495
- Num-num.
- Shoo.

363
00:14:22,528 --> 00:14:24,230
Go on, beat it.

364
00:14:24,263 --> 00:14:26,233
- Num-num.
- [Meows]

365
00:14:26,267 --> 00:14:28,235
- Whoa. It's a
'Peanut-Opie-Buster Parfait.'

366
00:14:28,268 --> 00:14:29,537
Ha, ha, ha!

367
00:14:29,570 --> 00:14:31,538
- Mike!
- Don't forget the cherry!

368
00:14:31,572 --> 00:14:33,507
- You nearly stepped on it!

369
00:14:33,540 --> 00:14:34,642
- On what?

370
00:14:34,675 --> 00:14:36,243
- You might've set it off.

371
00:14:36,277 --> 00:14:38,512
You really
must be more careful.

372
00:14:38,545 --> 00:14:40,580
- His burglar alarm.

373
00:14:40,613 --> 00:14:42,448
- How's it work?
Pretty good?

374
00:14:42,482 --> 00:14:44,618
- I don't know.
I never really tried it out.

375
00:14:44,652 --> 00:14:47,387
Only in theory.
In theory, it works fine.

376
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:48,620
- Well,
build a better mousetrap,

377
00:14:48,653 --> 00:14:50,992
and they'll
beat a path to your door,
they always say.

378
00:14:51,025 --> 00:14:52,392
- Shut up.
- Not 'mouse trap,'

379
00:14:52,425 --> 00:14:53,927
'burglar trap.'

380
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,595
I'm going to patent it.

381
00:14:55,628 --> 00:14:58,365
- Um, I'm gonna have to ask you
to start making sense here.

382
00:14:58,398 --> 00:15:00,167
- [Gasps]
Scatters! Look out!

383
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:02,703
- Am I nuts or something?

384
00:15:02,737 --> 00:15:05,005
- Huh, ooh, Puss-n-boots!
- [Growls Angrily]

385
00:15:05,038 --> 00:15:07,407
- I'll say.
- If you are...

386
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:09,142
We all are.

387
00:15:09,175 --> 00:15:11,578
- Ah,
this ain't good for me! Oh!

388
00:15:11,612 --> 00:15:13,280
- [Growls]

389
00:15:13,313 --> 00:15:16,683
- Uh, they never should've
delayed that spaying.

390
00:15:16,717 --> 00:15:18,418
- Got get him, Woof.
Sic 'em, boy!

391
00:15:18,452 --> 00:15:20,687
- Up yours, Opie.
I ain't goin'.

392
00:15:22,990 --> 00:15:25,158
- He'll make a great lap cat
for William Conrad.

393
00:15:25,192 --> 00:15:26,593
- [Chuckles]

394
00:15:29,195 --> 00:15:31,032
Oh, for dumb.

395
00:15:31,065 --> 00:15:33,467
Dumb, dumb, dumb, dumb.

396
00:15:33,500 --> 00:15:36,203
- Dumb, dumb, dumb-dumb, dumb.
- Atta boy Woof, sic 'em!

397
00:15:37,337 --> 00:15:39,172
- [Sighs]
- Well, that's over.

398
00:15:40,607 --> 00:15:43,643
- That cat was eating that.
- Diddley durhey.

399
00:15:43,677 --> 00:15:46,080
- What've we got here?

400
00:15:46,113 --> 00:15:47,715
- I suppose
the correct name would be

401
00:15:47,748 --> 00:15:51,385
'ammonia actride sulfate,
deethyly choloricin.'

402
00:15:51,418 --> 00:15:53,753
- [Southern Drawl]
And some other really
scientific stuff.

403
00:15:53,787 --> 00:15:56,223
- Perhaps
we ought to call it Goo.
Would that be simpler?

404
00:15:56,257 --> 00:15:57,725
- No, not really.

405
00:15:57,758 --> 00:15:59,192
- You know what?
- What?

406
00:15:59,225 --> 00:16:00,393
- That's what.
- Oh!

407
00:16:00,427 --> 00:16:02,062
- We're gonna make us
a million bucks.

408
00:16:02,095 --> 00:16:04,197
- I s'pose.

409
00:16:04,230 --> 00:16:07,067
- [Quacking]
- The million dollar ducks!

410
00:16:09,770 --> 00:16:11,203
- [Quack, Quack]

411
00:16:11,237 --> 00:16:14,073
- [As Groucho Marx]
Hey, this isn't kosher,
I should be eating this.

412
00:16:14,107 --> 00:16:16,610
- H.G. Wells'
'Food of the Ducks!'

413
00:16:16,643 --> 00:16:18,212
- [Quacking]

414
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:23,517
- Sorry we couldn't show you
the 'actual growing sequence.'

415
00:16:23,550 --> 00:16:25,085
- Oh, great.

416
00:16:25,118 --> 00:16:27,087
Now there's gonna be
duck stuff all over the yard.

417
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:30,490
- Can you imagine
if you fed this to cattle,
or-or to chickens?

418
00:16:30,523 --> 00:16:33,227
- Or Jim J. Bullock?
- Five, six times this size!

419
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:34,528
Imagine the money.

420
00:16:34,562 --> 00:16:36,397
Genius,
the first thing
you gotta do

421
00:16:36,430 --> 00:16:38,232
is make some more
of this stuff.

422
00:16:38,265 --> 00:16:40,100
- If he can remember
what he made it from.

423
00:16:40,133 --> 00:16:41,502
- Of course I can!

424
00:16:43,803 --> 00:16:45,638
- Oh boy,
we're going inside now!

425
00:16:45,672 --> 00:16:47,373
Hoop, dee doo,
dee doop, dee doo.

426
00:16:47,407 --> 00:16:49,042
- [Quack, Quack]

427
00:16:49,075 --> 00:16:50,543
- Go to the Dells,
ride the ducks!

428
00:16:50,577 --> 00:16:52,045
Ha, ha.

429
00:16:52,078 --> 00:16:53,647
- Huh? Rrr-rrr...

430
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,582
real chunks
of sodium diethylate.

431
00:16:55,615 --> 00:16:57,048
[Chewing Sounds]

432
00:16:57,082 --> 00:17:01,388
- [As Daffy Duck]
What sin could a duck commit
in a single lifetime?

433
00:17:01,422 --> 00:17:03,257
- [Humming]

434
00:17:03,290 --> 00:17:04,792
- Willow.
- Koruba!

435
00:17:04,825 --> 00:17:07,693
- First thing we'll do
is patent the formula.

436
00:17:07,727 --> 00:17:09,797
- First we find it.
- And market it.

437
00:17:09,830 --> 00:17:11,365
- Then we love!

438
00:17:11,398 --> 00:17:13,267
- Can you imagine the problems
we're gonna solve?

439
00:17:13,300 --> 00:17:16,270
Unlimited food supply
at practically no extra cost!

440
00:17:16,303 --> 00:17:18,138
Oh, and we gotta
keep this secret,

441
00:17:18,172 --> 00:17:20,740
- absolutely secret.
- Of course.

442
00:17:20,773 --> 00:17:23,177
- Mm, mm.
♪ The Wells Fargo wagon ♪

443
00:17:23,210 --> 00:17:25,278
♪ is-a-- ♪ Hm? Mm.

444
00:17:25,312 --> 00:17:28,415
- ♪ Comin' down... ♪
- All right, Woof.

445
00:17:30,250 --> 00:17:31,818
- Scarlotti?

446
00:17:31,852 --> 00:17:34,555
- [Deep Voice]
I wanna go walkies!

447
00:17:36,323 --> 00:17:38,825
[Dramatic Gulping Sounds
Mimicking Guitar Beats]

448
00:17:38,858 --> 00:17:41,228
- Well, come on in.
- [As Woof] I can't,

449
00:17:41,262 --> 00:17:43,563
- I'm a cheap effect.
- That's our freakish mishap.

450
00:17:43,597 --> 00:17:45,365
- He must've eaten
some of the Goo

451
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:46,700
when you fed the du--

452
00:17:46,733 --> 00:17:49,570
Oh, Mike!
The ducks are gone!

453
00:17:49,603 --> 00:17:51,305
Our secret's flown the coop!

454
00:17:51,338 --> 00:17:53,573
- [Mimicking Dramatic Music]

455
00:17:53,607 --> 00:17:56,310
- Oh, cool, Paris is burning.
- Okay to leave my stuff here?

456
00:17:56,343 --> 00:17:58,578
- Yeah, why not?
They close this place down,

457
00:17:58,612 --> 00:18:01,148
- nobody comes here anymore.
- Huh? The curtains are alive!

458
00:18:01,182 --> 00:18:02,482
- Boy I was sure dirty.

459
00:18:02,515 --> 00:18:04,785
I'm glad
we found this place
to clean up in.

460
00:18:04,818 --> 00:18:08,188
- [As Cowboy]
She cleaned up real nice, Pa.

461
00:18:08,222 --> 00:18:12,325
- [High Voice]
I tried soaking them out,
and scrubbing them out!

462
00:18:12,358 --> 00:18:14,327
- Hey aren't you guys
ready yet?

463
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:16,230
- I wanna go dancing!
- Boi-ing, Boi-ing!

464
00:18:16,263 --> 00:18:18,598
I'll go get some mud!

465
00:18:18,632 --> 00:18:21,335
It's hard to get
a matinée audience.

466
00:18:21,368 --> 00:18:22,602
- [Dying Noises]

467
00:18:25,238 --> 00:18:26,640
- Aha!
- Come on guys,

468
00:18:26,673 --> 00:18:28,608
I wanna do
my Andy Williams Revue!

469
00:18:28,642 --> 00:18:30,643
- Now what
is the story on you guys,

470
00:18:30,677 --> 00:18:34,247
- you're gonna kill yourselves!
- You like my Orlon sweater?

471
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:37,217
- Be ready in a minute.
- Wohahahahaoh!

472
00:18:37,250 --> 00:18:39,252
- Boy, this place
is really groovy!

473
00:18:39,285 --> 00:18:41,822
- Ha! Kids today.
- Hey ah, what?

474
00:18:41,855 --> 00:18:44,490
Are you girls
gonna take all night, huh?

475
00:18:44,523 --> 00:18:46,493
- I'm coming.
- No, you're combing.

476
00:18:46,527 --> 00:18:47,760
[Laughing]

477
00:18:47,793 --> 00:18:49,395
- Dig that nitty-gritty!

478
00:18:49,428 --> 00:18:51,532
- Stop slanging!
What are you saying?!

479
00:18:51,565 --> 00:18:52,867
[Chuckling]

480
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:54,500
That's a go-go!
Let's get over there.

481
00:18:54,533 --> 00:18:56,168
- Does she have bionic hearing?

482
00:18:56,202 --> 00:18:57,803
- ["When it Comes
to Your Love" playing]

483
00:18:57,837 --> 00:19:00,207
- It's the Beau Brummels!
- The Beau Bridges Brummels!

484
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:02,542
- The Beau Brummel Bridges
